WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.192 --> 00:00:03.359
(slow resonant music)

00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:08.715
- The weather's really in
your face in New Orleans.

00:00:09.736 --> 00:00:13.486
It is a character in
the play of New Orleans.

00:00:18.248 --> 00:00:19.763
This instrument, the weather warlock,

00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:23.153
is an audio mirror of
the sunrise and sunset,

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.637
so, theoretically, a blind person

00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:28.955
could experience the sunrise
and sunset through audio,

00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:30.038
in real time.

00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:33.977
My name is Quintron;
it's not my real name;

00:00:33.977 --> 00:00:36.731
it's a given musician's name.

00:00:36.731 --> 00:00:39.110
I definitely consider
myself, first and foremost,

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.679
to be a musician, but I'm also a builder

00:00:41.679 --> 00:00:45.325
and inventor of electronic
musical instruments,

00:00:45.325 --> 00:00:47.775
and the device that
we're talking about today

00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:49.341
is called the weather warlock,

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.801
which is weather-controlled analog synth.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.500
Right now, we're hearing
the sun just start

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.475
to activate the UV sensors

00:00:57.475 --> 00:00:59.725
on the outdoor sensor unit.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.871
That puttering sound is the sound

00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:05.497
of that sensor just
starting to get enough light

00:01:05.497 --> 00:01:07.580
to sonically activate it.

00:01:09.587 --> 00:01:13.050
It's using the weather to create music.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.924
There's no microphones; there's no,

00:01:14.924 --> 00:01:17.872
it's not the sound of rain.

00:01:17.872 --> 00:01:22.230
There are two components:
an inside set of brains,

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.365
which is the synthesizer part,

00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:27.411
and an outdoor set of sensors.

00:01:27.411 --> 00:01:29.808
There is a temperature sensor,

00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:33.168
which is effecting the speed of the drone,

00:01:33.168 --> 00:01:34.577
this drone.

00:01:34.577 --> 00:01:38.577
There is a set of wind
speed controlled sensors,

00:01:39.748 --> 00:01:41.904
the faster the wind blows,
the faster they activate

00:01:41.904 --> 00:01:43.250
these two notes.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.853
There is a moisture sensor, or rain,

00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:47.822
or humidity or snow.

00:01:47.822 --> 00:01:50.010
And the last one would be the sky sensor,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.143
which is a sensor at the top,

00:01:52.143 --> 00:01:54.932
a little periscope
that's aiming at the sky.

00:01:54.932 --> 00:01:56.696
So you can play it like
an instrument, too,

00:01:56.696 --> 00:01:58.128
you can just let it do it's thing,

00:01:58.128 --> 00:02:02.295
but I can also, you know,
change the timbre of the drone.

00:02:05.921 --> 00:02:08.669
So, sunrise is officially over,

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:11.419
according to the weather warlock.

00:02:13.042 --> 00:02:14.542
And everyone else.

00:02:18.711 --> 00:02:22.378
(resonant electronic drone)

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:26.653
Check one, two.

00:02:26.653 --> 00:02:31.203
Good evening, you are tuned
into weatherfortheblind.org,

00:02:31.203 --> 00:02:35.730
broadcasting, as usual, out
of New Orleans, Louisiana.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.487
The weather warlock has
become a live, 24/7,

00:02:40.487 --> 00:02:42.154
online musical feed.

00:02:43.372 --> 00:02:46.456
Sunrise was at 5:15 this morning,

00:02:46.456 --> 00:02:49.956
and sunset happening now, as you can hear,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.083
according to our UV sensors.

00:02:56.004 --> 00:02:59.322
This hasn't made me see
a sunset differently.

00:02:59.322 --> 00:03:01.405
You can just hear it now.

00:03:03.128 --> 00:03:06.211
(soft string music)

